{"width": 21, "active": 112, "test": {"name": "ui-supply-branches-owner-turn1", "kind": "rules", "opponent": "Human", "rounds": "4", "check": "supplyBranchesOwner", "rules": "sandbox", "question": "The owner's game, turn 1 (Red's network as Blue moves): clicking Red's truck at (-3,4) shows a thin branch to every supply unit fed through it now: the recon at (-6,5) (cut off without it) and the truck at (2,0), which links by driving to beside it (without it, it would drive 9 tiles to beside the truck at (0,8) instead). It used to show only the recon: branches were only for units cut off without it. The truck at (0,8): a branch to the truck at (8,0). For every supply unit or carrier of both sides, the branches (links shared, a pre-check) are exactly those the slow way draws (SupplyOverlay.DependentsReference: every linked unit's whole line). What the overlay keeps (SupplyLines): every line as SourcePath draws it; clicking four carriers works no network out again; a change of supply (Player.Resupply) works it out once. Kept as the owner saved it (fog on)."}, "day": 2, "factionSpecialUnits": "on", "fog": "on", "purchases": "on", "players": [{"personal_name": "Red", "id": 0, "displayColor": {"r": 1.0, "g": 0.0, "b": 0.0, "a": 1.0}, "factionName": "Federation", "AI": false, "aiProfile": "", "factionLocked": false, "money": 0, "eliminated": false, "eliminable": true, "team": 0}, {"personal_name": "Blue", "id": 112, "displayColor": {"r": 0.0, "g": 0.529411792755127, "b": 1.0, "a": 1.0}, "factionName": "Union", "AI": false, "aiProfile": "", "factionLocked": false, "money": 2000, "eliminated": false, "eliminable": true, "team": 0}], "tiles": [{"x": -10, "y": 10, "z": 0, "damage": 0, "combatCount": 0, "terrain": "Grassland"}, {"x": -10, "y": 9, "z": 1, "damage": 0, "combatCount": 0, "terrain": "Grassland"}, {"x": -10, "y": 8, "z": 2, "damage": 0, "combatCount": 0, "terrain": "Hills"}, {"x": -10, "y": 7, "z": 3, "damage": 0, "combatCount": 0, "terrain": "Grassland"}, {"x": -10, "